(3110900, 435093, 24528, '<td valign="top">This is in JFK Plaza in Philadelphia Pa.That building behind it is City Hall with William Penn on top. <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sfalice:</b></div><hr/><i> Terrific, a Jim Dine sculpture.  Haven''t seen one of those in waaay too long. I expect Dine would appreciate your juxtaposition of his work, slanted, with the spire you also include.  (Hint:  it also looks pretty darn good the way the artist presented it)  9 because I am so pleased to see it again.  I hope you will tell me where this version exists, later on. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'This is in JFK Plaza in Philadelphia Pa.That building behind it is City Hall with William Penn on top.  Originally posted by sfalice: Terrific, a Jim Dine sculpture.  Haven''t seen one of those in waaay too long. I expect Dine would appreciate your juxtaposition of his work, slanted, with the spire you also include.  (Hint:  it also looks pretty darn good the way the artist presented it)  9 because I am so pleased to see it again.  I hope you will tell me where this version exists, later on. ', '2006-12-13 00:18:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3110903, 434221, 69387, '<td valign="top">Beautiful photo! It feels like an illustration from a fairy tale book coming to life. Congratulations!</td>', 'Beautiful photo! It feels like an illustration from a fairy tale book coming to life. Congratulations!', '2006-12-13 00:19:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3110904, 435317, 67841, '<td valign="top">-<br/>Awww, fudge! Just when I thought I couldn''t do worst than my last entry...<br/> <br/>I still think it is an interesting macro - I was trying to make something that looked like a sun since the elements that exist inside every living thing once existed in the belly of a star (go ahead, look it up, we''re all made of stardust) - hence, "The Origins of Life".  <br/> <br/>Once I took the shot, I thought it looked like planet, or an egg, or a petri dish... - figured even if people didn''t get MY impression they might just have the imagination to make their own!<br/>-<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-08-26 10:46:58.</i></td>', '-Awww, fudge! Just when I thought I couldn''t do worst than my last entry... I still think it is an interesting macro - I was trying to make something that looked like a sun since the elements that exist inside every living thing once existed in the belly of a star (go ahead, look it up, we''re all made of stardust) - hence, "The Origins of Life".   Once I took the shot, I thought it looked like planet, or an egg, or a petri dish... - figured even if people didn''t get MY impression they might just have the imagination to make their own!-', '2006-12-13 00:19:29.000000', '2007-08-26 11:46:58.000000', 0),
(3110911, 435001, 35669, '<td valign="top">Would have been so damn pleasing had this won.  Love it<br/> <br/>well done, Nick</td>', 'Would have been so damn pleasing had this won.  Love it well done, Nick', '2006-12-13 00:21:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3110912, 434656, 42567, '<td valign="top">One of my fav''s on dpc!  Should have been in the top 5!<br/> <br/>Hey, top 10 now!  Congratulations<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-12-16 13:25:45.</i></td>', 'One of my fav''s on dpc!  Should have been in the top 5! Hey, top 10 now!  Congratulations', '2006-12-13 00:21:16.000000', '2006-12-16 13:25:45.000000', 0),
(3110913, 435001, 31133, '<td valign="top">Way to go on your highest score, Viktor! This picture was sooo perfect for the challenge, not to mention that it''s just a great image overall for all reasons. Whoooohoooo!</td>', 'Way to go on your highest score, Viktor! This picture was sooo perfect for the challenge, not to mention that it''s just a great image overall for all reasons. Whoooohoooo!', '2006-12-13 00:21:16.000000', NULL, 0),
