(3122340, 434221, 39057, '<td valign="top">I can''t believe that there is software that can do editing of EXif. This would mean DPC has not way to truly validate a date.</td>', 'I can''t believe that there is software that can do editing of EXif. This would mean DPC has not way to truly validate a date.', '2006-12-15 21:27:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3122511, 434866, 66635, '<td valign="top">Congrats!  I''m glad to see you ribbon.  Even if that guy hadn''t cheated, your pic was more deserving because his picture did not meet the challenge.  There was no celebrational aspect to it.  Whereas yours is dripping with celebration.  Good job!</td>', 'Congrats!  I''m glad to see you ribbon.  Even if that guy hadn''t cheated, your pic was more deserving because his picture did not meet the challenge.  There was no celebrational aspect to it.  Whereas yours is dripping with celebration.  Good job!', '2006-12-15 22:42:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3122629, 434866, 34938, '<td valign="top">this was my choice for the winner...so congrats on moving up to ribbon status...wish your image was on the front page a little longer...the cheats seem to make it bad for all of us. I have won two ribbons like you just have...thanks for sharing the outtakes as well...<br/> <br/>This image conveys life and vitality...the cheat''s one looked like death...I don''t know how the voters vote sometimes</td>', 'this was my choice for the winner...so congrats on moving up to ribbon status...wish your image was on the front page a little longer...the cheats seem to make it bad for all of us. I have won two ribbons like you just have...thanks for sharing the outtakes as well... This image conveys life and vitality...the cheat''s one looked like death...I don''t know how the voters vote sometimes', '2006-12-15 23:58:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3122704, 435244, 67841, '<td valign="top"><br/> <br/>Wow - you did a number on the voter''s with this one!  <br/> <br/>I have to admit, being the father of 5 &amp; having delivered the last one myself (and I do mean the LAST ONE - ha ha) I wasn''t that put off by this.  But, I didn''t score it high, either - in fact I gave it a 2 (sorry!).  Part of me did think it was a Brown attempt &amp; I wanted to oblige, but I had deeper reasons, too.<br/> <br/>I can appreciate a little shock value (hell, I did a series of "Things Found Dead &amp; Rotting" 10 years ago) but whenever I see an image I think of how it COULD have looked, I see the many roads the artist could have taken.  When I saw this one, I immediately thought that the cold sterility of it was absolutely meant to disgust and though I can appreciate that purpose &amp; admire its success, I also thought what if the lighting had been X &amp; the angle had been Y then my reaction would have been Z instead.  I know, I know - it''s not my place to ''own'' your art, but if it''s out there I WILL take it &amp; make it my own &amp; make those judgments ''cause it can be hard to that very same thing with my own.<br/> <br/>Anyway, I really wanted Z with this one, something that took a moment longer &amp; relished life instead flushing it down the toilet- too much of that going these days to begin with!  Perhaps you should have entered in Death instead...<br/> <br/>"Course what the f*** do I know - I shot a freaking LED bulb for a challenge about celebrating life.<br/> <br/><br/> <br/></td>', ' Wow - you did a number on the voter''s with this one!   I have to admit, being the father of 5 & having delivered the last one myself (and I do mean the LAST ONE - ha ha) I wasn''t that put off by this.  But, I didn''t score it high, either - in fact I gave it a 2 (sorry!).  Part of me did think it was a Brown attempt & I wanted to oblige, but I had deeper reasons, too. I can appreciate a little shock value (hell, I did a series of "Things Found Dead & Rotting" 10 years ago) but whenever I see an image I think of how it COULD have looked, I see the many roads the artist could have taken.  When I saw this one, I immediately thought that the cold sterility of it was absolutely meant to disgust and though I can appreciate that purpose & admire its success, I also thought what if the lighting had been X & the angle had been Y then my reaction would have been Z instead.  I know, I know - it''s not my place to ''own'' your art, but if it''s out there I WILL take it & make it my own & make those judgments ''cause it can be hard to that very same thing with my own. Anyway, I really wanted Z with this one, something that took a moment longer & relished life instead flushing it down the toilet- too much of that going these days to begin with!  Perhaps you should have entered in Death instead... "Course what the f*** do I know - I shot a freaking LED bulb for a challenge about celebrating life.  ', '2006-12-16 00:49:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3122722, 434866, 66635, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hotpasta:</b></div><hr/><i> this was my choice for the winner...so congrats on moving up to ribbon status...wish your image was on the front page a little longer...the cheats seem to make it bad for all of us. I have won two ribbons like you just have...thanks for sharing the outtakes as well...<br/> <br/>This image conveys life and vitality...the cheat''s one looked like death...I don''t know how the voters vote sometimes </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yeah, no kidding!  What''s up with people voting for images that have no connection to the challenge?  There were a lot of great images in this challenge that depicted life, but lacked any semblance of celebration.  Images that I would have given a 10 to, I gave a 5 to for not meeting the challenge.  And, believe me, I looked hard and gave the benefit of the doubt wherever even a hint or metaphor of a celbratory aspect could be found.</td>', 'Originally posted by hotpasta: this was my choice for the winner...so congrats on moving up to ribbon status...wish your image was on the front page a little longer...the cheats seem to make it bad for all of us. I have won two ribbons like you just have...thanks for sharing the outtakes as well... This image conveys life and vitality...the cheat''s one looked like death...I don''t know how the voters vote sometimes   Yeah, no kidding!  What''s up with people voting for images that have no connection to the challenge?  There were a lot of great images in this challenge that depicted life, but lacked any semblance of celebration.  Images that I would have given a 10 to, I gave a 5 to for not meeting the challenge.  And, believe me, I looked hard and gave the benefit of the doubt wherever even a hint or metaphor of a celbratory aspect could be found.', '2006-12-16 01:06:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3122768, 434129, 46885, '<td valign="top">Perhaps it''s a touch too abstract for the challenge, but the shot is awesome. I actually thought this was a tantalising body curve! (hinting at desire as a root of life). Great job - and with just an egg! Tells me to lift my backside and go shooting!</td>', 'Perhaps it''s a touch too abstract for the challenge, but the shot is awesome. I actually thought this was a tantalising body curve! (hinting at desire as a root of life). Great job - and with just an egg! Tells me to lift my backside and go shooting!', '2006-12-16 01:59:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(3122851, 434218, 26648, '<td valign="top">cool shot.</td>', 'cool shot.', '2006-12-16 04:58:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(3123005, 435212, 34192, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 9 during voting.  Probably taken by the limitless possibilities of story here.  I love that in an image - substance, purpose, point.  Something so fragile in this; makes it fit perfectly with the theme of the challenge.</td>', 'I gave this a 9 during voting.  Probably taken by the limitless possibilities of story here.  I love that in an image - substance, purpose, point.  Something so fragile in this; makes it fit perfectly with the theme of the challenge.', '2006-12-16 08:01:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(3123285, 434362, 66597, '<td valign="top">Hi Bob,<br/> <br/>First, please note you got six 10''s for this shot, which is great. In other words, a lot of people really love this photo! <br/> <br/>I''m middle-of-the road about this photo. What I love: the perspective, the expression, and the snow on the dog''s jowels. Really gives a great sense of playfulness and captures the essence of the moment. What kept me from scoring higher: I found the DOF a bit short (would love to have seen the eyes and ears in crisp focus) and wish that top ear were in photo. Finally - and I think this is the biggest element to me - the snow in the background is very bright and drew my eyes away from the subject. It may look different on different monitors, though. I''ve had that issue myself with several photos, especially my peacock love shot (looks great on my moniter and like absolute *&amp;$% on my hubby''s monitor). What I would suggest: perhaps try just a bit of dodging to the whites of your dog''s eyes (obviously not too much or he''ll end up looking like Casper the Ghost.)<br/> <br/>I realize how hard it is to put all those elements together when shooting animals, as the darn things just won''t stay still :-) <br/> <br/>Cheers,<br/>Noraneko<br/></td>', 'Hi Bob, First, please note you got six 10''s for this shot, which is great. In other words, a lot of people really love this photo!  I''m middle-of-the road about this photo. What I love: the perspective, the expression, and the snow on the dog''s jowels. Really gives a great sense of playfulness and captures the essence of the moment. What kept me from scoring higher: I found the DOF a bit short (would love to have seen the eyes and ears in crisp focus) and wish that top ear were in photo. Finally - and I think this is the biggest element to me - the snow in the background is very bright and drew my eyes away from the subject. It may look different on different monitors, though. I''ve had that issue myself with several photos, especially my peacock love shot (looks great on my moniter and like absolute *&$% on my hubby''s monitor). What I would suggest: perhaps try just a bit of dodging to the whites of your dog''s eyes (obviously not too much or he''ll end up looking like Casper the Ghost.) I realize how hard it is to put all those elements together when shooting animals, as the darn things just won''t stay still :-)  Cheers,Noraneko', '2006-12-16 10:00:13.000000', NULL, 0),
