(3123573, 434866, 14386, '<td valign="top">I just saw this.  CONGRATULATIONS!  You desrve the ribbon.  And you''re right about the "jumping in the beach" note.  We never know who the original is.  But what we are sure is that this picture is a very good one.  Congratulations again.:)<br/> <br/>Manny</td>', 'I just saw this.  CONGRATULATIONS!  You desrve the ribbon.  And you''re right about the "jumping in the beach" note.  We never know who the original is.  But what we are sure is that this picture is a very good one.  Congratulations again.:) Manny', '2006-12-16 13:36:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3124187, 434656, 32767, '<td valign="top">WOW! What a great image glad I got to see it. Nice placing though I think it should have done much better but that''s no surprise. There are people out there that have a knee-jerk reaction to some things and if they thought you were preaching that may have been why you got nailed (pardon the pun) with a few 3''s.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-12-16 20:03:04.</i></td>', 'WOW! What a great image glad I got to see it. Nice placing though I think it should have done much better but that''s no surprise. There are people out there that have a knee-jerk reaction to some things and if they thought you were preaching that may have been why you got nailed (pardon the pun) with a few 3''s.', '2006-12-16 20:01:41.000000', '2006-12-16 20:03:04.000000', 0),
(3124327, 434362, 60862, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by noraneko:</b></div><hr/><i>Finally - and I think this is the biggest element to me - the snow in the background is very bright and drew my eyes away from the subject.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Just to prove ya can''t please everyone, I thought the snow was one of the strongest things going for this shot.  A nice, simple background helps the subject stand out.<br/> <br/>That said, I agree with everything else noraneko said. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by noraneko:Finally - and I think this is the biggest element to me - the snow in the background is very bright and drew my eyes away from the subject.  Just to prove ya can''t please everyone, I thought the snow was one of the strongest things going for this shot.  A nice, simple background helps the subject stand out. That said, I agree with everything else noraneko said. :)', '2006-12-16 20:56:26.000000', NULL, 0),
